[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TC-H1FWHVPS-
TITLE: Test Protocol

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-18
TITLE: Grid control clock - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall be able to generate an output for a grid control clock at a frequency between 1
kHz and 20 kHz. Also, current output of an emission will be different from existing / non-existing
grid control clock.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* A treatment plan should be ready to load.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Load a 20 second treatment plan.
3. Start the emission.
4. Wait for 5 seconds.
5. Wait another 10 seconds.
6. Check if the grid counter clock is present.
7. Check the emission's current.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
3. Verify the emission started.
4. Record the current of emission.
5. Record the current of emission.
6. Verify the grid counter clock is present, and its frequency is between 1-20 kHz.
7. Verify the emission's current is <0.2 mA.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-1
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-19
TITLE: High voltage setpoint 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When user loads a treatment plan and it is ready for running, make sure the firmware provides and
sets the high voltage setpoint.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* A treatment plan should be ready to load.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Load a 20 second treatment plan.
3. Check the state of the system.
4. Check the value of the reported high voltage.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
3. Verify its state is Ready.
4. Record the value and verify it's within 10% of loaded treatment target.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-17
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-20
TITLE: Main control reporting - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is powered on, LED TBD on mainboard should pulse at a rate much faster than
1 Hz.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Check LED TBD on the Main Board.
3. Measure the pulsing of the LED TBD on the Main board.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify it's pulsing.
3. Verify it's pulsing at a rate much faster than 1 Hz.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-4
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-21
TITLE: HVPS digital status signals - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is powered, the service user should check the reported value of HVPS digital
signals in the Service screen with / without a running treatment plan.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* The user of the system needs to be a service user.
* A treatment plan should be ready to load.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Click Services symbol in the left side of the screen.
3. Look for HVPS digital signal's value in the service screen.
4. Load a treatment plan.
5. Look for HVPS digital signal's value in the service screen.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify the service screen displayed.
3. Record the value and verify HV status should indicate no HV.
4. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
5. Record the value and verify HV status should indicate HV.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-5
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
