[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-30
TITLE: Control loop - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system powered on and started to run the loaded treatment plan, make sure the firmware
provided a control loop to automatically adjust output parameters during emission to establish a
stable and smooth emission.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* A treatment plan should be ready to load.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Load a 20 second treatment plan. Record the value of TBD before starting the emission.
3. Start the emission.
4. Wait for 5 seconds.
5. Wait another 10 seconds.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
3. Verify the emission started.
4. Record the value of TBD.
5. Record the value of TBD.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-14
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-31
TITLE: PC Communication 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is powered on, the user can send a request through firmware to run bootloader
application and load a new set of firmware through the USB.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* Bootloader application should be loaded in the USB and should be present for user to run it.
* A new set of firmware should be in the USB.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Run bootloader application through USB.
3. Click Logs symbol in the left-hand side of screen.
4. Check the utility log.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully and there is not any treatment plan loaded into system.
2. Verify the application started to run.
3. Verify the logs displayed in the middle of screen.
4. Record the utility log and verify system enters into bootloader mode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-15
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-32
TITLE: PC Communication 2 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system is powered on, the user can send a request through firmware to erase a
predetermined area of flash memory, corresponding to application CRC verification area when
requested by the PC.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* A new set of firmware should be in the USB.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Run bootloader application through USB.
3. Click Logs symbol in the left-hand side of screen.
4. Check the utility log.
5. Check the USB free space.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully and there is not any treatment plan loaded into system.
2. Verify the application started to run.
3. Verify the logs displayed in the middle of screen.
4. Record the utility log and verify system enters into bootloader mode.
5. Verify an area in the USB which was corresponded to application CRC verification area was erased.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-16
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-33
TITLE: Filament current ramping - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The user powered on the system, loaded a treatment plan. Then after warmup procedure, user has
to make sure the warm up is logged in the system.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and ready to use.
* A treatment plan is ready to load.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system.
2. Load a treatment plan.
3. Check the state of the system.
4. Wait till the Warmup procedure is finished.
5. Click the Logs symbol in the left side of the screen.
6. Check the logs.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on successfully.
2. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
3. Verify its state is Warmup.
4. Verify the status of the system is not Warmup anymore.
5. Verify the logs displayed in the screen.
6. Verify the log for readings of the filament current ramp up during the warmup procedure. Values in the log should indicate a ramp rate of less than 1A/sec.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-8
  ROLE: Verifies

